[B]0.4.0 reconstruction update:[/B] Recovered click windows/exclusions, camera and sensitivity state, scoped join/teleport exclusions, ordered entity acknowledgements, scaffold geometry and proxy message formats. The complete source-equivalence objective remains open; see [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/FIDELITY.md]the fidelity ledger[/URL]. Fresh and historical test results are separated in the validation report.

[B]Further 0.4.0 behavior:[/B] FastPlace uses first-placement batches with late trigger inclusion; GhostHand uses neighboring bed materials and can cancel accepted enclosed-bed breaks (checks.ghosthand-a.cancel). Set that option false for monitoring. Timer windows and millisecond balance preserve recovered packet authority. Vehicle/web/crowding ages advance only on position packets. Separate cumulative history survives successful automatic VL reset. Missing textual settings inherit shipped defaults during upgrades. The complete-fidelity ledger remains authoritative for unfinished scopes.

[B]0.5.0 behavior:[/B] Combat uses raw sequence clocks, bounded relative-target history and acknowledged velocity prediction. Packet checks retain frame latches and source-specific material/event ages. FastBreak uses SURVIVAL interaction timing and actual break-event authority. Hit suppression defaults to zero damage; settings.cancel-hits-cancel-event selects cancellation. Automatic command dispatch starts a configurable player-wide cooldown; accepted reload, reset, logout and disable cancel pending automatic actions. LinoAlertEvent can cancel local staff chat independently of other violation actions. The full reconstruction remains in progress; the fidelity ledger lists unresolved behavior.
